    "confidence": 0.8,
    "explanation": "This dispute is about the SGD 4.00 cancellation fee on trip TRP-00206, and both of you have described what happened accurately, so the case is decidable on the papers.\n\nThe fee cannot stand under POL-NS-01. That clause is conjunctive - it needs all four limbs - and three of them fail on this trip's own records. Limb (b): the driver's GPS trace never places him within the 120 m arrival radius for this LARGE_VENUE pickup; his closest fix to the pin is 284.95 m. Limb (c): there is no in-geofence dwell at all - 0 qualifying fixes and a longest qualifying run of 0 seconds against the 300-second minimum. Limb (d): the trip was terminated by the driver with reason code DRIVER_UNABLE_TO_LOCATE, which is not RIDER_NO_SHOW, RIDER_UNREACHABLE or EXCESSIVE_WAIT; POL-NS-01 itself treats that code as the driver's admission that he could not find the rider and routes such a trip to POL-NS-03.\n\nPOL-NS-03 therefore governs, and the driver's claim under it is allowed. The driver was stationary for the required dwell - 6.6 minutes, comfortably over the 300-second LARGE_VENUE minimum - at a point outside the 120 m arrival radius but well inside the 400 m ceiling, at 284.95 m. On those facts he did not arrive at the pickup point and the cancellation fee is refunded to the rider in full: SGD 4.00. The rider's alternative route under POL-NS-02 reaches the same result, but POL-NS-02 expressly yields to POL-NS-03 on exactly these facts, and POL-NS-06's in-geofence shortfall (0 seconds against 300) independently requires the same full refund.\n\nWho absorbs the driver's cost is a separate question, and POL-NS-03 answers it from the chat log. The log holds only two SYSTEM notifications, and neither party named an entrance, block, tower or bay. The venue has 4 registered pickup points, so limb (ii) applies: the mislocation is attributed to pin ambiguity rather than to either party, and the driver receives a platform-funded goodwill payment of 50 percent of the fee - SGD 2.00 - charged to the platform and never recovered from the rider. The rider's SGD 4.00 refund and the driver's SGD 2.00 payment are independent and are not netted against each other.\n\nOn the remaining points. No false-arrival referral is recorded: at the 15:12:05 arrival marker the driver was 284.95 m from the pin, under POL-NS-05's 300 m threshold, and stationary, and POL-NS-05 expressly routes a stationary driver within 300 m but outside the arrival radius to POL-NS-03. POL-NS-07's 80 percent driver compensation (SGD 3.20) is not payable, because that clause operates only where POL-NS-01 is satisfied in full, which it is not; and in any event the anti-farming check does not trip (no_show_terminations_30d of 1 against completed_trips_30d of 187). POL-NS-06's limb (i) accumulation route is closed because the traffic advisory EV-ADVIS-00206-01 is MISSING (weight 0.0, MISSING_ARTIFACT), and nothing is available to sum in any case. POL-NS-04 is not engaged: the chat log contains no rider message, so its exoneration route cannot be made out; but the rider's own track places her within 22.5 m of the pin throughout the window, and her presence is not in issue.\n\nNothing here requires escalation. The GPS trace carries a weight of 0.8 for issue LOW_SAMPLE_RATE (median 18 s sampling against a nominal 10 s cadence), but that tag is schema-level only and satisfies no limb of POL-NS-08: the largest interval is 26 s against the 120 s threshold, there are 52 fixes against a 6-fix minimum, and the gaps list is empty. Because the fact that decides this case - the driver's position relative to the pin - is carried by that trace at 0.8, my confidence is capped at 0.8, which is above the 0.70 escalation floor. The chat log's message count and msg_id numbering are complete, and the SGD 4.00 fee reconciles with the LARGE_VENUE zone fee and the RYDE_X tier fee under the resolution rule, so there is no POL-NS-08(c) or (d) defect. No POL-NS-09 trigger fires."
  },
  "discarded_claims": [
    {
      "claim": "The trace's schema-level impairment is not a policy-level impairment and should not push this case to a reviewer. No limb of POL-NS-08 bites: the largest sampling interval is 26 s against the 120 s gap threshold and the gaps list is empty; the trace holds 52 fixes against the 6-fix minimum and 31 rider fixes; the chat log's 2 messages match trip_record.chat_message_count of 2 with contiguous msg_ids; and the 4.00 cancellation fee reconciles with the LARGE_VENUE zone fee and the RYDE_X tier fee, so there is no fare defect. POL-GEN-02's confidence cap is therefore not dragged below the 0.70 floor, and in any event the deciding fact is carried on two independent artifacts - the GPS trace at 0.8 and the trip record at 1.0 - so the cap is the maximum, 1.0. No limb of POL-NS-09 is engaged and the case is decidable on the papers.",
      "side": "RIDER",
      "reason": "POL-GEN-02(1) disclosure defect. The claim cites EV-GPS-00206, whose weight_multiplier is 0.8 (issue code LOW_SAMPLE_RATE). It states that the trace is impaired but does not name the issue code that fired, so the disclosure POL-GEN-02(1) requires - the artifact is impaired AND which issue codes fired - is incomplete. Claim discarded."
    },
    {
      "claim": "POL-NS-07's 80 per cent driver compensation is not available on this record. That clause operates only 'where POL-NS-01 is satisfied in full', which cannot be said where limb (b) and limb (d) both fail. The driver's only route to money, if any, is the platform-funded half-fee goodwill in POL-NS-03(ii), which cannot be charged back to the rider. The rider should not be paying a $3.20 driver compensation out of a $4.00 fee for a pickup the driver never reached, and the fare ledger should show nothing taken from her.",
      "side": "RIDER",
      "reason": "POL-GEN-02(1) disclosure defect. The claim cites EV-GPS-00206, whose weight_multiplier is 0.8 (issue code LOW_SAMPLE_RATE), and is entirely silent about that impairment - it neither states that the artifact is impaired nor names the issue code. Silence discards the claim."
    }
  ]
}
